\f0\b \cf0 IN THE BOX\
\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 Every part (except an active GPS helix SMA antenna) needed to build a finished node. Nothing is soldered and nothing is flashed.\
\pard\tx720\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \
\
- Bare 82 mm PCB, all modules and headers, 8 GB microSD\
- Printed enclosure, TPU seals, all hardware and wiring\
- WiFi & LoRa SMA antennas, U.FL pigtails and bulkheads, factory ceramic UFL GPS antenna\
- Fan, thermal switch, power switch, waterproof USB-C panel jack, UPS charger board, JST terminals and cables\
\

\f0\b You supply: two 18650 flat top batteries, active GPS SMA antenna, soldering tools.
\f1\b0 \
\
\

\f0\b BUILD IT
\f1\b0 \
\
1. Work through the assembly manual end to end. It has photographed steps for the soldering, the connectors, the enclosure, and all wiring:\
\
	github.com/lukeswitz/AntiHunter \'96 hw folder, Antihunter-DIGINODE-AssemblyManual.pdf\
\
2. 
\f0\b Two modules need a header modification first, covered on page 6 of that manual
\f1\b0 : the RTC ships with female headers, and some tamper sensors ship with inverted 90 degree headers.\
\
3. Fit the SD card before you close the case. The slot is not reachable once the PCB is mounted.\
\

\f0\b FLASH IT
\f1\b0 \
\
4. Flash the Heltec V3.2 with the latest stable Meshtastic from flasher.meshtastic.org, then 
\f0\b set the serial module: Enabled, mode TEXT MSG, baud 115200, pins 19 RX / 20 TX
\f1\b0 . Without this the node and the radio cannot talk. 
\f0\b Use the meshtastic_config.py script in the /scripts folder of the repo to automate this process.
\f1\b0 \
\
5. Flash AntiHunter on the ESP32 over USB. Web flasher: lukeswitz.github.io/AntiHunter. Pick Full for the web UI, or Headless for quiet field ops with no WiFi AP. \
\
6. Set the LoRa region, change the Bluetooth pairing pin, and make your own encrypted channel primary with the public default off.\
\
7. Full firmware: join the 
\f0\b Antihunter
\f1\b0  WiFi AP, password 
\f0\b antihunt3r123
\f1\b0 , open http://192.168.4.1 and change those credentials first.\
\
\

\f0\b POWER
\f1\b0 \
\
Regulated 5 V only, from USB or the UPS board. Never wire cells or an unregulated supply to the PCB. A 2 A fast-blow fuse in the battery line is recommended and is not supplied. One USB cable at a time: the ESP32 and the radio share the power rails.\
\
\

